  "servings": 4,
  "description": "This shakshuka recipe features gently poached eggs in a flavorful tomato and red pepper sauce. Try it for an easy, healthy breakfast, lunch, or dinner!",
  "notes": "Cover the pan for perfectly cooked eggs. It will help the egg whites cook through while keeping the yolks runny. If you don't have a lid for your pan, you can cover it with a baking sheet. If you prefer to use fresh tomatoes, replace the canned ones with 4 cups diced fresh tomatoes. Feel free to skip the cayenne if you're sensitive to heat.",
